namespace jo

//[ The contract for the program entry point
  !
  ! The entry point is the one top-level function named `main` that takes no
  ! parameters. It must return `Unit` and may receive only the context
  ! parameters declared here and those that a build binds with `--provide`.
  ! It is an error if no such function exists. If several do, name the entry
  ! point explicitly by passing `--link jo.main=app.main` to the compiler.
  !
  ! The `receives` clause lists the capabilities the runtime makes available to
  ! the entry point. It is not a requirement: a `main` that uses only some of
  ! them — or none at all — still conforms. See the Entry Point section of the
  ! language documentation.
  !
  ! There is no standard input capability. A program that reads input obtains it
  ! from a backend-specific API, such as `py.input`, and passes it on as its own
  ! context parameter.
  !
  ! The `pass` body is only a placeholder, so that this declaration is a
  ! well-formed deferred function; the program supplies the real entry point.
//]
defer def main: Unit receives IO.stdout, IO.stderr, IO.args = pass
